ARTICLE 1 — DEFINITIONS AND INTERPRETATION

For the purposes of this Agreement:

1.1. Software: Computer programs, applications, source code, executable files, interfaces, designs, documentation, updates, databases and associated materials owned or legally controlled by the Licensor.

1.2. Licensor: SYNTARA Technologies, acting as the owner or authorised distributor of the Software.

1.3. Licensee: Any individual, business, organisation or legal entity granted permission to access or use the Software.

1.4. Source Code: Human-readable programming instructions, scripts, algorithms and associated development materials used to create or maintain the Software.

1.5. Object Code: The compiled or otherwise machine-readable form of the Software.

1.6. Derivative Work: A modification, adaptation, translation, transformation or other work based upon protected elements of the original Software.

1.7. Written Permission: Explicit authorisation issued by an authorised representative of SYNTARA Technologies through a verifiable written communication or legally valid agreement.

1.8. Intellectual Property: Copyrights, trademarks, patents, trade secrets, software architecture, proprietary designs and other legally protected intellectual assets.

1.9. Commercial Use: Use of the Software in business operations, commercial services, revenue-generating activities or other activities governed by a commercial licence.

1.10. Confidential Information: Non-public technical, commercial or operational information belonging to the Licensor.

