ARTICLE 4 — RESTRICTED ACTIVITIES

Unless expressly authorised in writing by the Licensor, the Licensee shall not:

4.1. Modify, alter, adapt or create derivative works from protected portions of the Software.

4.2. Redistribute, republish, sublicense or resell the Software.

4.3. Reproduce or distribute substantial portions of proprietary source code.

4.4. Claim ownership of the Software or its original components.

4.5. Remove, conceal or falsify copyright notices, trademarks or proprietary identification.

4.6. Transfer licence credentials or access rights to unauthorised third parties.

4.7. Develop and distribute unauthorised derivative products incorporating protected elements of the Software.

4.8. Circumvent legitimate licence verification systems, access controls or technical protection mechanisms, except where applicable law permits.

4.9. Reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble the Software, except where such restrictions are prohibited by applicable law.

4.10. Use the Software or confidential materials to misrepresent ownership or authorship.

