8.1. Unauthorised modification, reproduction, distribution or exploitation of protected Software may constitute a breach of this Agreement and, where applicable, copyright infringement.

8.2. SYNTARA Technologies proposes liquidated damages of USD $12,000 (Twelve Thousand United States Dollars) for each qualifying breach involving unauthorised modification of protected Software.

8.3. The parties intend this amount to represent a reasonable pre-estimate of potential losses, including investigation, intellectual-property protection, remediation and commercial damage arising from the defined breach.

8.4. The amount shall be enforceable only to the extent permitted by applicable law. Its reasonableness and enforceability may be determined by a competent court.

8.5. A qualifying breach must be established using appropriate evidence and legal procedures.

8.6. The Licensor reserves the right to pursue other remedies available under applicable copyright and intellectual-property laws, subject to applicable restrictions against double recovery.

8.7. This provision does not establish an automatic government-imposed fine or authorise the Licensor to impose financial penalties without lawful grounds.

8.8. Nothing in this Article limits rights or exceptions that cannot legally be restricted.

